Z||000012||Sage||11-26-2001||10:25 AM||||We had the same situation.  Wanted to have a car that wasn't a Fiero so we could carry 4 people comfortably and have plenty of trunk space, enough power to keep up on the interstate, but still get good gas mileage AND not break the bank.<P>We looked around a while and finally decided on a used Grand Prix.  Fit all the criteria and are very happy with the choice.  Took it to Daytona in August and was probably the most enjoyable long haul we've had in a long while.  <P>3.1 with 4 spd. auto w/overdrive, power sun roof, power drivers seat, tilt, cruise, air and radio controls in the steering wheel,(yes they work)!  Clean, well maintained, good looking, comfortable car that we got for under $3,000!  Put tires on it and replaced the top dogbones, other than that, routine maintenance.<P>Very happy with this choice.<P>Just my .02!<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
