Z||000014||hugh||11-26-2001||09:22 PM||||If you really want something like a GN,how much more will it cost to insure it?If you subtract what you have to spend to insure a newer car(which you have to pay anyway) from what it costs to insure a GN,That is your real cost!Also,T-Types are the same car mechanically.They just don't have the mystic the GN has.||||reg||14
Z||000015||Master_Sushi||11-26-2001||09:27 PM||||I second the Impala SS! My dad use to have one of these, talk about a manly car. A huge car with jumbo wheels, a hot 350, low to the ground, and all stock! They are collector cars now. If you are going to get on get the 96. The 96 is the best year for a few little reasons. Driving this car was a blast. Everybody gave 2nd looks because it looks so much like an unmarked cop. Even more so since it was black <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I only wish I could have dricen it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">, I was to young at the time tho.....<P>You could also get a nice mid-90 saab 9000 turbo. With the 5 speed they are quite fast, and get great mileage.||||reg||14
Z||000016||Red2m4||11-26-2001||10:21 PM||||I'll put on my flame suit and recomend a Ford Crown Victoria/Mercury Gran Marquis.  Lots of power for a large car, (Same drivetrain as a mustang GT, I think, so lots of performance goodies if you wanted them.) lots of space.  Very nice ride and I get 26mpg on the highway, maybe 21 around town.  Good value too...<P>Also, if you come up behind someone on the expressway, they sometimes slowdown and changelanes !||||reg||10
Z||000017||frontal lobe||11-27-2001||01:38 AM||||Red2m4 is right.  Crown Vic/Merc marquis are real sleeper cars.  Lots of room.  Decent reliability.  Pretty good engine and handling.  Only thing is can you handle the image??<P>Nissan Maxima's are a little tight in the back, but a pretty snappy car and very reliable.<BR>||||reg||1
